    "result_text": "All 269 tests pass with BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented sequential membership numbers for newly created owners, returned as the integer field `membershipNumber` in the owner response.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipNumber` (int32) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `membershipNumber` field (`@Column(name = \"membership_number\")`) with getter/setter so it persists and is returned on GET.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`h2`, `hsqldb`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added the `membership_number` column to the `owners` table. Also updated the hsqldb `data.sql` seed inserts (positional `INSERT INTO owners VALUES`) with a trailing `NULL` to match the new column count.\n\n4. **`AssignMembershipNumber.java`** (new OfficeFloor function) \u2014 Reads the built `@Val Owner`, counts existing owners via `OwnerRepository.findAll().size()`, and sets `membershipNumber = count + 1`.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 Wired the new `assignMembershipNumber` step (under `transaction` governance) into the pipeline between the duplicate checks and `save`.\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` maps `membershipNumber` automatically by name (entity \u2192 DTO), so both the POST create response and the GET response include it. The Cp09 invariant (two consecutive creations differ by exactly one) holds because the newly-saved owner is flushed and counted before the next creation within the transaction.",
